{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And He will save, the tents of Judah</b> — those encamped with the enemy, for thus is the way of armies: they dwell in tents around the city." "<b>House of David</b> — to this day in the city of Baghdad, capital of Ishmael, they are the heads of the exile, a large and great family with a book of genealogy from ancient years. And this is its meaning: for first, before the salvation of Jerusalem, HaShem will save the tents of Judah, who are outside the city with the enemy camps, in the manner He said above: <i>upon the house of Judah I will open My eyes</i> and <i>every horse of the peoples I will strike with blindness</i>. And why will He first save the tents of Judah?" "<b>So that it not be magnified</b> — lest the house of David and the inhabitants of Jerusalem, who are inside the city with the Messiah, be able to boast, and lest their glory be magnified over the children of Judah — <i>our hand saved you</i>."], :book :zechariah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {1 "The word 'years' (שנים) may intend 'years of antiquity'; rendered literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zecharia -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zecharya"] ["1" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=25&perek=5&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:46:57.731731013Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}